<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mike Vardy has spent his career inside the word &#8220;productivity.&#8221; He built frameworks around it, taught it, made a living off it. And for years the word itself bugged him. But don&#8217;t forget &#8220;Productivity&#8221; started out as a term for measuring the efficiency of factories.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mike argues the better word is &#8220;productiveness&#8221;. Not how much you produce, but whether what you produce, and how you go about producing it, actually amounts to something.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That distinction is the subject of <a href="https://mikevardy.com/productiveness">Mike&#8217;s new book</a>, out now. Nine principles for keeping meaningful work sustainable once the systems around it start to strain. My congratulations to Mike for getting this book published.</p>
